-- title:
--   p-adic approximation: Λᵥ=(Λ⊗ 1)+p^kΛᵥ
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ which is finitely generated and whose $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $D$ (a full lattice). Let $p$ be a prime natural number, let $v$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that the image of $p$ lies in the prime ideal attached to $v$ (so $v$ is the place above $p$), and let $k$ be a natural number. Write $\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda\,v$ for the additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z \otimes c$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of the adic completion $\mathbb{Q}_v$. Then for every $Y$ in this subgroup there exist $z \in \Lambda$ and $E$ again in $\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda\,v$ with
--   $$Y = z \otimes 1 + \bigl(1 \otimes p^{k}\bigr)\, E,$$
--   the product being taken in the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$. Equivalently, $\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda\,v = (\Lambda \otimes 1) + (1 \otimes p^{k})\,\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda\,v$, so that the global lattice is dense in its completion.
--
--   This is the standard strong-approximation-free statement that a full $\mathbb{Z}$-lattice in a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra is dense in its $v$-adic completion, in the explicit form needed to correct an element of the completed lattice by a global element modulo $p^k$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, in the analysis of level-$U$ Hecke data and of maximal orders and order coordinates for quaternion algebras.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Submodule_exists_mem_add_one_tmul_pow_mul_of_mem_localBox.lean

